commit e0905b3d3c06282a17d63bd4ddc9eac68424ab56
Author: thawk105 <thawk105@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Sep 19 22:23:41 2026 +0900

    perf(mocc): defer payload witness formatting until after unlock

    Capture post-store producers while the write locks are held and emit S
    records after unlockCLL. Preserve witness grammar and decode failures
    without adding include lines or changing TRACE=0 executable source.

    The T-1943 payload-lineage witness wrote each S record (decode + ofstream
    formatting) between the tidword publish and unlockCLL, which lengthens the
    [publish, unlock] window that the T-2774 static candidate (ii) must cross.
    This change keeps the shared-body decode (and its abort on decode failure)
    at the publish site, stores the decoded producer in a thread_local vector
    that is only constructed when the witness is enabled, and formats the S
    records after unlockCLL by re-walking write_set_ in the same order. Values,
    count, order and the 5-field S grammar are unchanged; consumers that check
    witness-post-store-token-mismatch keep their coverage. Static design and
    rationale: izanagi output/insights/2026-09-18/t2779-mocc-g2-observation-conditions
